# ThreadSanitizer cannot see the synchronisation inside libavcodec and
# libavutil: those are stock shared libraries built without
# instrumentation, and an AVBufferRef's reference count is an atomic
# compiled into them. TSan sees the two writes - a frame-threading
# worker allocating, the decode thread releasing - and no ordering
# between them, so it reports a race that the reference count in fact
# orders.
#
# Suppressed by library rather than by call site, so a race in this
# core's own code is still reported. Building ffmpeg with TSan would
# be the way to check the libraries themselves, which is not what this
# sample is for: it is here for the core's audio pipe.
race:libavcodec.so
race:libavutil.so
race:libavformat.so
race:libswresample.so
race:av_buffer_unref
race:av_buffer_replace
